  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition" corresp="#Ed">
    <body>
      <div type="mūlam" rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="TNV7">
      <l>murukaṉu miraviyu māyaṉum vēntaṉum</l>
<l>varuṇaṉu<anchor xml:id="varunan"/> māka vakuttaṉar koḷalē.<anchor xml:id="kolale"/></l></lg>
<lg xml:lang="en">
  <l>Murukaṉ, Iravi, Māyaṉ, Vēntaṉ, and Varuṇaṉ</l> 
  <l> – [let there be an] understanding that they have assigned [them as the gods].</l></lg>
</div>
</body>
</text>
<text xml:lang="ta" type="edition" corresp="#Ed">
    <body>
      <head xml:lang="en">Commentary</head>
      <div type="commentary" rend="parallel">
      <p xml:id="TNV7comm1">eṉpatu collap paṭṭa karuviṉ uḷ atiteyvam ām āṟuṇarttutaṉutaliṟṟu.</p>
       <p xml:lang="en">The quoted [<term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">cūttiram</hi></term>] intends to make known the way in which the
       presiding deities occur amongst the aforementioned constituent elements.</p></div>
       <div type="commentary" rend="parallel">
      <p xml:id="TNV7comm2">murukavēḷum<anchor xml:id="murukavel"/> pakalōṉumāyaṉum intiraṉum<anchor xml:id="intiran"/> varuṇaṉumuṟaiyāṉē yain tiṇaikkum atiteyvam ām eṉṟa vāṟu. <num>7.</num></p>
      <p xml:lang="en">Murukavēḷ, Pakalōṉ, Māyaṉ, Intiraṉ, and Varuṇaṉ are the presiding deities for the five poetic settings according to the [established] order.</p></div>
      </body>
      </text>
      <standOff type="notes1" corresp="#TNV7comm2"><note xml:lang="ta" target="#murukavel"><term xml:lang="en">Cf. IAC1, p. 25:</term> kuṟiñcikkut teyvam murukavēḷ</note>
      <note xml:lang="ta" target="#intiran"><term xml:lang="en">Cf. IAC1, p. 27:</term> marutukkut teyvam intiraṉ</note></standOff>
